[{"role": "system", "content": "\nYou are a programming expert. \nYou will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. \n\nYour task is summarize the modifications made in the patch.\nYour summary should consist of two parts, modifications in each file and their relationships.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "From 30f347ae7cc1178c431f968a89d4b4a375bc0d39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Yang Yingliang <yangyingliang@huawei.com>\nDate: Sat, 27 Mar 2021 17:33:22 +0800\nSubject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: fix missing unlock on error in stmmac_suspend()\n\nAdd the missing unlock before return from stmmac_suspend()\nin the error handling case.\n\nFixes: 5ec55823438e (\"net: stmmac: add clocks management for gmac driver\")\nReported-by: Hulk Robot <hulkci@huawei.com>\nSigned-off-by: Yang Yingliang <yangyingliang@huawei.com>\nSigned-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>\n\ndiff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c\nindex 3a4f0c2d42a3..d34388b1ffcc 100644\n--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c\n+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c\n@@ -5964,8 +5964,10 @@ int stmmac_suspend(struct device *dev)\n \t\t/* Disable clock in case of PWM is off */\n \t\tclk_disable_unprepare(priv->plat->clk_ptp_ref);\n \t\tret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);\n-\t\tif (ret)\n+\t\tif (ret) {\n+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n+\t\t}\n \t}\n \n \tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);\n-- \n2.25.1\n\n\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "### Modifications in Each File\n\n**File Modified: `drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c`**\n- In the `stmmac_suspend` function, an additional line of code was added to unlock a mutex (`mutex_unlock(&priv->lock)`) before returning an error code (`return ret;`) when the `pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev)` call fails. This change ensures that the mutex is properly released in the error handling case.\n\n### Relationships\n- The modification addresses a bug related to missing mutex unlocking in the `stmmac_suspend` function, which could lead to potential deadlocks or resource contention if the function exits without releasing the lock. The fix is directly related to the error handling logic introduced in a previous commit (identified by the Fixes tag), ensuring that the mutex is always unlocked before returning from the function in case of an error."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"llm_patch_file_names": ["drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c"]}, "begin to deal with drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c in strategy1", {"full_context_length": 74}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.\n        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.\n\n        Root cause:\n        The bug was caused by a missing mutex unlock operation in the error handling path of the `stmmac_suspend` function. When the function encountered an error during the `pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev)` call, it returned the error code without releasing the mutex, which could lead to a deadlock situation if the lock remained held while other parts of the code attempted to acquire it.\n        \n        Commit message:\n        net: stmmac: fix missing unlock on error in stmmac_suspend()\n\nAdd the missing unlock before return from stmmac_suspend()\nin the error handling case.\n\nFixes: 5ec55823438e (\"net: stmmac: add clocks management for gmac driver\")\nReported-by: Hulk Robot <hulkci@huawei.com>\nSigned-off-by: Yang Yingliang <yangyingliang@huawei.com>\nSigned-off-by: David S. Miller <davem@davemloft.net>  \n        \n        Patch:\n          */\n int stmmac_suspend(struct device *dev)\n {\n \tstruct net_device *ndev = dev_get_drvdata(dev);\n \tstruct stmmac_priv *priv = netdev_priv(ndev);\n \tu32 chan;\n \tint ret;\n \n \tif (!ndev || !netif_running(ndev))\n \t\treturn 0;\n \n \tphylink_mac_change(priv->phylink, false);\n \n \tmutex_lock(&priv->lock);\n \n \tnetif_device_detach(ndev);\n \n \tstmmac_disable_all_queues(priv);\n \n \tfor (chan = 0; chan < priv->plat->tx_queues_to_use; chan++)\n \t\thrtimer_cancel(&priv->tx_queue[chan].txtimer);\n \n \tif (priv->eee_enabled) {\n \t\tpriv->tx_path_in_lpi_mode = false;\n \t\tdel_timer_sync(&priv->eee_ctrl_timer);\n \t}\n \n \t/* Stop TX/RX DMA */\n \tstmmac_stop_all_dma(priv);\n \n \tif (priv->plat->serdes_powerdown)\n \t\tpriv->plat->serdes_powerdown(ndev, priv->plat->bsp_priv);\n \n \t/* Enable Power down mode by programming the PMT regs */\n \tif (device_may_wakeup(priv->device) && priv->plat->pmt) {\n \t\tstmmac_pmt(priv, priv->hw, priv->wolopts);\n \t\tpriv->irq_wake = 1;\n \t} else {\n \t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);\n \t\trtnl_lock();\n \t\tif (device_may_wakeup(priv->device))\n \t\t\tphylink_speed_down(priv->phylink, false);\n \t\tphylink_stop(priv->phylink);\n \t\trtnl_unlock();\n \t\tmutex_lock(&priv->lock);\n \n \t\tstmmac_mac_set(priv, priv->ioaddr, false);\n \t\tpinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state(priv->device);\n \t\t/* Disable clock in case of PWM is off */\n \t\tclk_disable_unprepare(priv->plat->clk_ptp_ref);\n \t\tret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);\n-\t\tif (ret)\n+\t\tif (ret) {\n+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n+\t\t}\n \t}\n \n \tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);\n \n \tif (priv->dma_cap.fpesel) {\n \t\t/* Disable FPE */\n \t\tstmmac_fpe_configure(priv, priv->ioaddr,\n \t\t\t\t     priv->plat->tx_queues_to_use,\n \t\t\t\t     priv->plat->rx_queues_to_use, false);\n \n \t\tstmmac_fpe_handshake(priv, false);\n \t}\n \n \tpriv->speed = SPEED_UNKNOWN;\n \treturn 0;\n }\n EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(stmmac_suspend);\n\n        \n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n```c\n-\t\tif (ret)\n+\t\tif (ret) {\n+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);\n \t\t\treturn ret;\n+\t\t}\n```"}, {"s1_raw_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "-\t\tif (ret)", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 5967, "induce_cid": "5ec55823438e850c91c6b92aec93fb04ebde29e2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tif (ret) {", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 5967, "induce_cid": "5ec55823438e850c91c6b92aec93fb04ebde29e2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 436, "induce_cid": "0867bb9768dedaae2c0e572ade5ccaa682a9298c"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 456, "induce_cid": "29555fa3de865630570b5f53c847b953413daf1a"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 5954, "induce_cid": "134cc4cefad34d8d24670d8a911b59c3b89c6731"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 5971, "induce_cid": "29555fa3de865630570b5f53c847b953413daf1a"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 6039, "induce_cid": "29555fa3de865630570b5f53c847b953413daf1a"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\t\tmutex_unlock(&priv->lock);", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 6086, "induce_cid": "134cc4cefad34d8d24670d8a911b59c3b89c6731"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 129, "induce_cid": "5ec55823438e850c91c6b92aec93fb04ebde29e2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 133, "induce_cid": "5ec55823438e850c91c6b92aec93fb04ebde29e2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 140, "induce_cid": "b4d45aee6635197d257f3469413837cd94fc11f4"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 150, "induce_cid": "5ec55823438e850c91c6b92aec93fb04ebde29e2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 1183, "induce_cid": "74371272f97fd1a7b668f1da34aea4ae737c2fa1"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 1290, "induce_cid": "286a837217204b1ef105e3a554d0757e4fdfaac1"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 1614, "induce_cid": "71fedb0198cbbdacc7e2d6b95e124a3821b5dca2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 1693, "induce_cid": "71fedb0198cbbdacc7e2d6b95e124a3821b5dca2"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 1702, "induce_cid": "56329137211639528ddf05c59a9d7cbde6879d1f"}, {"buggy_stmt": "return ret;", "file_name": "drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c", "lineno": 1883, "induce_cid": "71fedb0198cbb